:"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"blind_id\":\"C069\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":0.5,\"reason\":\"Places the identifier in the listed ETF class name, marketing and disclosures, and warns against labelling non-ETF siblings or sub-funds as ETFs. It does not list the constitution, prospectus and KID/KIID as required documents. It does not clearly state that the ETF sub-fund in a mixed umbrella must be identified. It also omits, and in effect denies, the option to use the identifier at sub-fund level, offering class-level identification only.\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":\"\\\"Do not call the whole sub-fund an ETF if it also has non-ETF classes\\\": this conflicts with Reg. 88(2) and CBI Q&A, which allow the identifier at sub-fund level or listed-class level for sub-funds with listed and unlisted classes, provided the classes are clearly distinguished. It is a material falsehood about the sub-fund-level option. It is not the listed central anchor, which concerns sub-fund-only identification or labelling non-ETF siblings as ETFs.\",\"grade\":\"partial\",\"rationale\":\"The answer gets the listed-class identification and the non-ETF sibling caution right, and it commits no listed central error. However, the document coverage is incomplete, mixed-umbrella sub-fund identification is not explicit, and it wrongly excludes sub-fund-level use of the identifier. Coverage of 0.5 out of 1 required point meets the partial threshold, and the material local falsehood caps the grade at partial in any case.\"}","ttft_ms":5093,"type":"result","duration_ms":9443,"uuid":"815ec6bd-ed94-4545-a8e8-323fe1c363b9","ttft_stream_ms":1572,"time_to_request_ms":62,"first_content_frame_ms":1572,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
